{
  "@context": {
    "rdfs": "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#",
    "label": "rdfs:label",
    "comment": "rdfs:comment",
    "isDefinedBy": { "@id": "rdfs:isDefinedBy", "@type": "@id" }
  },
  "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns",
  "label": "bootstrap's diagram elements",
  "comment": "The elements bootstrap's diagrams add to BPMN, in the XML namespace https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns# and written with the prefix bootstrap.processes:, the name of the Subgraph that declares them. A reader matches them by this namespace, never by the prefix text.",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns#skill",
      "@type": "rdfs:Class",
      "label": "skill",
      "comment": "On a task: a Skill the task requires, the responsibility an Actor carries out to complete it. Attribute ref: the Skill's name, a file in skills/. A task may carry several. The task names the Skill and the Skill names no task; a graph export states it as dcterms:requires. A diagram that uses it declares it as <bpmn:extension definition=\"bootstrap.processes:skill\" mustUnderstand=\"false\"/>.",
      "isDefinedBy": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns#role",
      "@type": "rdfs:Class",
      "label": "role",
      "comment": "On a lane, only as variable=\"true\": the lane's performer is whoever invoked the process, and saying so is a decision rather than an omission. Every other lane names its Role with BPMN's own partitionElementRef, pointing at a top-level bpmn:resource whose id is the Role's id in scenarios/roles.json. A lane names a Role; it is not one (owner, 2026-10-16). Attribute ref is retired: readers accept it, with a warning, for one release.",
      "isDefinedBy": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns#precondition",
      "@type": "rdfs:Class",
      "label": "precondition",
      "comment": "On a process: what must hold before it starts, as text — or, with attribute before, the id of a task in that process, what must hold before that task starts (a task drawn earlier in the process establishes it). Attribute kind: stated (nothing can observe it, so it is never reported as satisfied) or checkable (a check can decide it). A checkable one names its check, for example check=\"file-exists\" with ref, the file, as a path relative to the instance that holds the diagram and inside it.",
      "isDefinedBy": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns"
    }
  ]
}
